 ball","dish/pork-ball"],["Rechao","dish/rechao"],["Shuangbaotai","dish/shuangbaotai"],["Small sausage in large sausage","dish/small-sausage-in-large-sausage"],["Taiwanese beef noodle soup","dish/taiwanese-beef-noodle-soup"],["Taiwanese fried chicken","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken"],["Taiwanese fried chicken cutlet","dish/taiwanese-fried-chicken-cutlet"],["Tàⁿ-á-mī","dish/ta-a-mi"],["Tapioca Express","dish/tapioca-express"],["Tea egg","dish/tea-egg"],["Ti-hueh-kué","dish/ti-hueh-kue"],["Tshik-á-mī","dish/tshik-a-mi"],["Tube rice pudding","dish/tube-rice-pudding"],["Xiaolongbao","dish/xiaolongbao"]]}]},"ingredient/zea-mays-saccharata-group":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/zea-mays-saccharata-group","n":"Zea mays Saccharata Group","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Sweet corn (Zea mays convar. saccharata var. rugosa), also called sweetcorn, sugar corn, pole corn, or simply corn is a variety of corn (maize) grown for human consumption with a relatively high sugar content."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-zea-mays-saccharata-group"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_corn"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"]]],["Wampanoag foodways","cuisine/wampanoag-foodways",[["Succotash","dish/succotash"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Bell peppers","ingredient/bell-peppers"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Edible salt","ingredient/edible-salt"],["Lima bean","ingredient/lima-bean"],["Sweet corn","ingredient/sweet-corn"],["Tomatoes","ingredient/tomatoes"]]}]},"dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls","n":"Egg puffs and soup pearls","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Egg puffs and soup pearls are choux-pastry pellets, resembling chickpea seeds, that are popular in Central Europe. They are typically used to garnish soups, but can be used to decorate other kinds of food, including desserts, or eaten alone as snacks. Egg puffs are baked, whereas soup pearls are deep-fried."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg_puffs_and_soup_pearls"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Austrian cuisine","cuisine/austrian-cuisine"],["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine"],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia"],["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Vienna Sunday Kitchen","ref":"site/vienna-sunday-kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"vienna-sunday.kitchen","note":"Viennese food blog of Austrian home cooking and pastries, with English-language recipes.","url":"https://www.vienna-sunday.kitchen/newest-recipes/","suggested":true},{"name":"Lil Vienna","ref":"site/lilvienna-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lilvienna.com","note":"Austrian recipes from Ursula and David, two Austrians living in Boston.","url":"https://www.lilvienna.com/?p=1366","suggested":true},{"name":"Quick German Recipes","ref":"site/quick-german-recipes-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"quick-german-recipes.com","note":"Long-running site by German-born cook Gerhild Fulson (Oma) with traditional German home recipes.","url":"https://www.quick-german-recipes.com/about-me.html","suggested":true},{"name":"Dirndl Kitchen","ref":"site/dirndlkitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dirndlkitchen.com","note":"Blog of German and Bavarian recipes, from main dishes to holiday baking.","url":"https://dirndlkitchen.com","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Austrian cuisine","links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chicken paprikash","dish/chicken-paprikash"],["Dampfnudel","dish/dampfnudel"],["Gulyásleves","dish/gulyasleves"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Liptauer","dish/liptauer"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Potato salad","dish/potato-salad"],["Sachertorte","dish/sachertorte"],["Spätzle","dish/spatzle"],["Strudel","dish/strudel"],["Tarhonya","dish/tarhonya"],["Zopf","dish/zopf"]]}]},"dish/em-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/em-restaurant","n":"Em (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Em is a fine dining restaurant in the Condesa area of Mexico City that serves contemporary Mexican cuisine with Japanese influences. It has daily à la carte options and an eight-to nine-full-course tasting menu. It is owned by chef Luis \"Lucho\" Martínez, who opened it in 2018 as Emília in Mexico City's Colonia Cuauhtémoc district. The business was later renamed and relocated to Colonia Roma due to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on the food industry. Critics have given Em favorable reviews, and in 2024, the restaurant received one Michelin star in the first Michelin Guide covering restaurants in Mexico. The restaurant was relocated to Condesa in 2026."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-em-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":tru